--- FINDINGS.md cites mock/Cargo.toml:44-52 ---
  44: # arvo's cost is in monomorphised output, not in source it could reuse: the
  45: # per-width, per-strategy, per-sign impl macros turn a small file into an
  46: # enormous object, and `libarvo_strategy.rlib` alone was 19 MB. Incremental
  47: # caches a dep graph proportional to that output on every rustc invocation and
  48: # cargo garbage-collects the sessions lazily, so an afternoon of iteration put
  49: # 8.9 GB in `target/debug/incremental` across a thousand session directories.
  50: #
  51: # It buys correspondingly little: the expensive part is re-monomorphising, which
  52: # incremental does not avoid. Kept for whatever is built here next.
